RING\n8. CIVIL ENGINEERING\n9. THERMAL ENGINEERING\n10. MECHATRONICS ENGINEERING\n11. AUTOMATION AND CONTROL ENGINEERING\n12. ENVIRONMENTAL ENGINEERING\n13. TELECOMMUNICATIONS ENGINEERING\n14. COMPUTER SCIENCE\n15. ECONOMICS AND MANAGEMENT\n16. EDUCATIONAL MANAGEMENT\n17. FOOD TECHNOLOGY\nARTICULATION\n1. Electrical and Electronics Engineering Technology\n2. Automotive Engineering Technology\n3. Construction Engineering Technology\n4. Printing Engineering Technology\n5. Machine Manufacturing Technology\nRESEARCH\nINTRODUCTION\nJOURNAL OF TECHNICAL EDUCATION SCIENCE\nSCIENTIFIC RESEARCH ACTIVITIES\nSTUDENTS' ACTIVITIES\nLECTURERS' ACTIVITIES\nOUTREACH\nENTERPRISE RELATIONS\nINTERNATIONAL RELATIONS\nALUMNI\nABOUT ALUMNI COMMUNITY\nALUMNI EVENTS\nHo Chi Minh City University of Technology and Education has been renamed Ho Chi Minh City University of Technology and Engineering (HCM-UTE) under Decision No. 2809/QĐ-TTg issued by the Prime Minister. Smart governnance & Empowering the HCM-UTE brand.\nNews\nHCM-UTE Signs Memoranda of Understanding with Seven Legal Practice Organizations, Expanding Internship Opportunities for Law Students\nDate 02/10/2026\nHCM-UTE Attends the 2026 University–Enterprise Cooperation Forum and Shares Its Model of Co-creating Value with Industry\n30/09/2026\nHCM-UTE Works with Yaskawa to Review More Than Two Years of the Yaskawa Mechatro Lab and Plan Its Second Phase\n28/09/2026\nHCM-UTE Equips Final-Year Students with Labor Law Knowledge before They Enter the Job Market\n23/09/2026\nSee all\nInternational Projects\nHCMUTE Organized the International Conference on Mechatronics Technology (ICMT 2025) – An Academic Forum Connecting Global Knowledge\nDate 13/11/2025\nThe Opening of the Asian Graduate Studies Summit (A-GRASS 2025) at HCMUTE\n30/05/2025\nHCMUTE Launches GreenEdAsia Project: Advancing Green Transition in Southeast Asian Higher Education\n17/02/2025\nHCMUTE hosts the final round of the 2024 Ho Chi Minh city AI Challenge\n22/10/2024\nSee all\nHCM-UTE Successfully Hosts GTSD 2026, Advancing Green Technology and Sustainable Development\nOn July 30–31, 2026, Ho Chi Minh City University of Technology and Engineering (HCM-UTE, formerly Ho Chi Minh City University of Technology and Education) successfully hosted The 8th International Conference on Green Technology and Sustainable Development (GTSD 2026).\nHCM-UTE Signed MOU with the VNU-HCM Dormitory and Urban Area Management Center to Strengthen Student Support\nOn the morning of August 13, 2026, Ho Chi Minh City University of Technology and Engineering (HCM-UTE, formerly Ho Chi Minh City University of Technology and Education) held a signing ceremony for a Memorandum of Understanding (MOU) and an exchange session on experience in space leasing and utilization with the Dormitory and Urban Area Management Center of Vietnam National University Ho Chi Minh City (VNU-HCM).\nHCM-UTE – Mahasarakham University (Thailand) Academic Exchange Program Concludes with Research for Sustainable Development\nAs part of the international cooperation program between Ho Chi Minh City University of Technology and Engineering (HCM-UTE, formerly Ho Chi Minh City University of Technology and Education) and Mahasarakham University (MSU), Thailand, the Faculty of Foreign Languages at HCM-UTE, in collaboration with several academic faculties, organized an academic exchange program for 30 students from Mahasarakham University from July 6–9, 2026.\nHCMUTE Alumni Sports Festival 2025: A Gathering of Sportsmanship and Connection with HCMUTE\nWith the desire to create a healthy and meaningful sports playground while strengthening the bonds among generations of alumni, faculty, and businesses, on September 21, 2025, the Alumni Association of Ho Chi Minh City University of Technology and Education (HCMUTE) organized the 2025 Alumni Sports Festival, attracting the enthusiastic participation of nearly 200 athletes from various units, enterprises, and alumni groups.\nHCMUTE Trade Union Brought a Loving Mid-Autumn Festival to the Children of Staff and Employees\nIn harmony with the joyful spirit of the Mid-Autumn Festival, on the evening of October 3, 2025 (the 12th day of the 8th lunar month), the Trade Union of Ho Chi Minh City University of Technology and Education (HCMUTE) organized the “Mid-Autumn Festival Night 2025” program for the children of the university’s staff and employees.\nVisit month:\n10,445\nVisit total:\n316,896\nCopyright © 2013, HCMC University of Technology and Engineering\nAdd:\nNo 1 Vo Van Ngan Street, Thu Duc Ward, Ho Chi Minh City\nTel:\n(+84 - 028) 38968641 - (+84 -028) 38961333 - (+84 -028) 37221223\nFax:\n(+84 - 028) 38964922\nE-mail:\noia@hcmute.edu.vn"
